# NETGEAR R8000 (bcm53xx / brcmfmac) -- v2 SQM (bufferbloat control)
# Workstream: modern roaming/steering/QoS. Rationale/evidence: ../../notes.md
#
# NO QUEUES ARE PRE-DECLARED IN THIS FILE (FINDINGS.md #56). Two earlier
# versions of this file both got this wrong in a way worth recording:
#   - The original version hardcoded a queue to the physical 'wan' port,
#     which this deployment's WiFi-extender architecture pivot left
#     physically unplugged (FINDINGS.md #55) - zero real shaping.
#   - The #55 fix replaced that with two queues hardcoded to this
#     deployment's CURRENT uplink names (american_wwan/american24_wwan).
#     That is wrong for the same reason this project never hardcodes to a
#     specific client - it happens to be "American" today, but nothing
#     about SQM should ever know or care what the uplink is called.
#
# etc/hotplug.d/iface/32-dynamic-wan-sqm is now the sole owner of every
# queue section here. On every ifup, it walks ALL firewall zones generically
# (config/firewall) looking for `option masq '1'` - this router's own,
# already-existing, name-agnostic definition of "this is a NAT'd uplink
# zone", true for the original wired 'wan' zone exactly as much as the
# current 'american' zone, and for any future zone added the same way. For
# whichever logical interface(s) are members of such a zone and currently
# up, it auto-creates (first time only - never overwrites an existing
# section) a `sqm_<logical-interface-name>` queue with a generic,
# identity-agnostic seed bandwidth, then rebinds `option interface` (a RAW
# DEVICE NAME to sqm-scripts, confirmed by reading its own
# src/run-openwrt.sh directly - no logical-name resolution, no hotplug
# reaction of its own) to whatever the current real device is - device
# names are NOT stable across reboots (phy0->phy3->phy6->phy12...,
# repeatedly observed this session).
#
# Once a real per-link measurement is taken (same solo-throughput ablation
# methodology as FINDINGS.md #52/#55), refine that specific
# `sqm_<interface>` section's download/upload via UCI directly - the
# hotplug script only ever sets the seed values on FIRST sight of a new
# interface name, so a real measurement, once entered, survives every
# future boot untouched.
#
# Package: sqm-scripts (pulls in kmod-sched-cake, kmod-ifb, tc, ip,
# iptables-mod-ipopt automatically -- see ../../imagebuilder-packages.md).
